{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoArgSector","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoArgSector","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoBranchByArgument"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.sa_lt_cb_nonvacuous","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.sa_lt_cb_nonvacuous","kind":"theorem","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoArgSector.lean#L314-L335","doc":"**Non-vacuity for `sa_lt_cb`.** The hypotheses are satisfiable, and by a point\nthat is genuinely on the arc: `R = 2` lies inside the measured range\n`[1.2821, 2.3247]` of `‖y₂‖²` over the complex-pair arc (Route 28). Solving the\ntwo Vieta relations at `R = 2` gives `a = 1/2`, then `c = 3/4`, then\n`b = √7/2`, `s = √7/4`, and the conclusion reads `√7/8 < 3√7/8`.\n\nThe check with real content is Route 28, which verifies both Vieta relations,\n`1 < R`, and the conclusion at 700 points of the arc at 40 dps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.branchInt_eq_zero_of_roots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.branchInt_eq_zero_of_roots","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoArgSector.lean#L293-L310","doc":"**The pinning, with the sector hypotheses discharged from the root data.**\n\n`t` is the positive real root, `y₂` and `y₃` the other two. Only two facts about\nthem are used: `y₃` is pushed into the closed lower half plane by `x`, and — when\n`φ > π/2` — so is `y₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_mul_conj_root_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_mul_conj_root_neg","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoArgSector.lean#L280-L291","doc":"**The lower member of the conjugate pair is pushed into the open lower half\nplane**: `Im(x · conj y) < 0`. This is `sa_lt_cb` with the components named. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.sa_lt_cb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.sa_lt_cb","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoArgSector.lean#L195-L276","doc":"**Route 27's obligation, proved: `s·a < c·b`.**\n\n`y₂ = a + b i` with `b > 0` is the upper member of the conjugate pair,\n`R = ‖y₂‖²`, `c = cos φ`, `s = sin φ > 0`. The hypotheses are Vieta consequences:\n`h1` is `e₁ = 2c` with the real root written as `1/R`, and `h2` is `e₂ − e₁ = 1`\ncleared of denominators.\n\nRoute 27 measured `max(s·a − c·b) = −0.3365` over the arc and left this open.\nThree sign certificates discharge it; see the module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.one_lt_normSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.one_lt_normSq","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoArgSector.lean#L177-L193","doc":"**`‖y₂‖² > 1` for the conjugate pair** — equivalently, the real root `1/R` is\nbelow `1`.\n\nFrom the Vieta relation alone: `b² > 0` forces `4R(R−1)² > (R²−R−1)²`, and on\n`(0,1]` the left side is at most `16/27` — certificate `(3R−1)²(4−3R) ≥ 0` —\nwhile the right side is at least `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.lt_of_sq_lt_of_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.lt_of_sq_lt_of_pos","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoArgSector.lean#L173-L175","doc":"From `u² < v²` with `0 < u`, `0 < v`, conclude `u < v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.lt_of_sq_gt_of_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.lt_of_sq_gt_of_neg","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoArgSector.lean#L166-L171","doc":"From `v² < u²` with `u, v < 0`, conclude `u < v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.sq_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.sq_gap","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoArgSector.lean#L160-L164","doc":"The bridge: on the constraint set `(s·a)² − (c·b)² = a² − c²R`, so the sign of\n`a² − c²R` decides `s·a` against `c·b` once their own signs are known. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_nonneg_of_im_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_nonneg_of_im_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoArgSector.lean#L153-L156","doc":"**A root pushed into the closed lower half plane gives a nonnegative\nargument.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_pos_real_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.arg_pos_real_root","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoArgSector.lean#L130-L151","doc":"**The positive real root lands in the open right half plane.**\n\nIf `y₁ = t` is real with `0 < t < 1` and `x` sits on the unit circle with\n`Im x > 0`, then `1 − t·x` has positive real part — because `‖t·x‖ = t < 1` — and\nnegative imaginary part, so its argument lies in `(−π/2, 0)`.\n\nThis is the only use of `y₁ < 1`, and it is what replaces Route 27's measured\nminimum `−1.4077` against `−π/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.branchInt_eq_zero_of_sector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.branchInt_eq_zero_of_sector","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoArgSector.lean#L114-L126","doc":"**The pinning, from the sector data.** Compare\n`branchDiff_eq_zero_of_continuousOn`, which needs continuity plus a base point,\nand `branchInt_eq_zero_of_arg_structure`, which needs Route 27's three\ninequalities: this needs neither. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.sum_window","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.sum_window","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoArgSector.lean#L98-L112","doc":"**The window, from the sector data.**\n\n`a₁` is the argument at the positive real root, confined to `(−π/2, 0)` because\nthat root has modulus `< 1`. `a₃` is nonnegative. `a₂` is free — except when\n`φ > π/2`, which is exactly where the slack below `φ − 2π` runs out. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.branchInt_eq_zero_of_window","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.branchInt_eq_zero_of_window","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoArgSector.lean#L84-L96","doc":"**The branch integer is `0` as soon as the argument sum lies in a window of\nradius `2π` about `φ`.**\n\nWeaker than `branchInt_eq_zero_of_bounds`, which fixes the window at `(−π, 2π)`;\nhere it may follow `φ`, and that is the whole gain. ","signatureChunk":0}]}